Table full name: HTAN_2.HTAN.SCHEMA_CURRENT
Column name: Attribute Type: TEXT Description: Key characteristic X of the assay, related protocol, or downstream data that we want to record as metadata feature.
Column name: Description Type: TEXT Description: Provide a definition or a reference containing the definition of attribute X. Preferably provide a source ontology link or code in addition to the definition. Leave blank if the final description is pending.
Column name: Parent Type: TEXT Description: Parent class of this attribute - i.e. where to 'hook' this attribute into an existing schema. Note that this assumes a single existing schema/a single json-ld schema context; if we need to support classes/attributes/properties defined across multiple schemas/json-ld contexts we'd need to add a schema/context column that specifies the context of each attribute, if different from the context of the attribute's parent.
Sample rows:
[{'Attribute': 'Component', 'Description': 'Category of metadata (e.g. Diagnosis, Biospecimen, scRNA-seq Level 1, etc.); provide the same one for all items/rows.', 'Parent': None}, {'Attribute': 'Spike In Concentration', 'Description': 'The final concentration or dilution (for commercial sets) of the spike in mix [PMID:21816910]', 'Parent': 'ERCC'}, {'Attribute': 'HTAN Parent Data File ID', 'Description': 'HTAN Data File Identifier indicating the file(s) from which these files were derived', 'Parent': 'File'}, {'Attribute': 'PhysicalSizeXUnit', 'Description': 'The units of the physical size of a pixel. See OME enumeration of allowed values for the UnitsLength attribute -- default: microns (um)', 'Parent': 'Imaging'}, {'Attribute': 'Imaging Object Class Description', 'Description': 'Free text description of object class [string]', 'Parent': 'Imaging'}]

